            "output": "<path>/Users/aasheesh/Documents/webdev/os/cli/docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Sessions and Checkpoints\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: Entire CLI creates checkpoints for AI coding sessions. The system is agent-agnostic - it works with Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, or any tool that triggers Entire hooks.\n6: \n7: ## Domain Model\n8: \n9: ### Session\n10: \n11: A **Session** is a unit of work. Defined in `strategy/session.go`:\n12: \n13: ```go\n14: type Session struct {\n15:     ID          string       // e.g., \"2025-12-01-8f76b0e8-b8f1-4a87-9186-848bdd83d62e\"\n16:     Description string       // Human-readable summary (first prompt or derived)\n17:     Strategy    string       // Strategy that created this session\n18:     StartTime   time.Time\n19:     Checkpoints []Checkpoint\n20: }\n21: ```\n22: \n23: ### Checkpoint\n24: \n25: A **Checkpoint** captures a point-in-time within a session. Defined in `strategy/session.go`:\n26: \n27: ```go\n28: type Checkpoint struct {\n29:     CheckpointID     id.CheckpointID // Stable 12-hex-char identifier\n30:     Message          string          // Commit message or checkpoint description\n31:     Timestamp        time.Time\n32:     IsTaskCheckpoint bool            // Task checkpoint (subagent) vs session checkpoint\n33:     ToolUseID        string          // Tool use ID for task checkpoints (empty for session)\n34: }\n35: ```\n36: \n37: ### Checkpoint Types\n38: \n39: The low-level `checkpoint.Type` (from `checkpoint/checkpoint.go`) indicates storage location:\n40: \n41: ```go\n42: type Type int\n43: \n44: const (\n45:     Temporary Type = iota // Full state snapshot, shadow branch\n46:     Committed             // Metadata + commit ref, entire/checkpoints/v1\n47: )\n48: ```\n49: \n50: | Type | Contents | Use Case |\n51: |------|----------|----------|\n52: | Temporary | Full state (code + metadata) | Intra-session rewind, pre-commit |\n53: | Committed | Metadata + commit reference | Permanent record, post-commit rewind |\n54: \n55: ## Interface\n56: \n57: ### Session Operations\n58: \n59: Sessions are accessed via standalone functions in `strategy/session.go`:\n60: \n61: ```go\n62: // ListSessions returns all sessions from entire/checkpoints/v1,\n63: // plus additional sessions from strategies implementing SessionSource.\n64: func ListSessions() ([]Session, error)\n65: \n66: // GetSession finds a session by ID (supports prefix matching).\n67: func GetSession(sessionID string) (*Session, error)\n68: ```\n69: \n70: ### Checkpoint Storage (Low-Level)\n71: \n72: The `checkpoint.Store` interface (from `checkpoint/checkpoint.go`) provides primitives for reading/writing checkpoints. Used by strategies.\n73: \n74: ```go\n75: type Store interface {\n76:     // Temporary checkpoint operations (shadow branches - full state)\n77:     WriteTemporary(ctx context.Context, opts WriteTemporaryOptions) (WriteTemporaryResult, error)\n78:     ReadTemporary(ctx context.Context, baseCommit, worktreeID string) (*ReadTemporaryResult, error)\n79:     ListTemporary(ctx context.Context) ([]TemporaryInfo, error)\n80: \n81:     // Committed checkpoint operations (entire/checkpoints/v1 branch - metadata only)\n82:     WriteCommitted(ctx context.Context, opts WriteCommittedOptions) error\n83:     ReadCommitted(ctx context.Context, checkpointID id.CheckpointID) (*CheckpointSummary, error)\n84:     ReadSessionContent(ctx context.Context, checkpointID id.CheckpointID, sessionIndex int) (*SessionContent, error)\n85:     ReadSessionContentByID(ctx context.Context, checkpointID id.CheckpointID, sessionID string) (*SessionContent, error)\n86:     ListCommitted(ctx context.Context) ([]CommittedInfo, error)\n87: }\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Key option types (abbreviated):\n91: \n92: ```go\n93: type WriteTemporaryOptions struct {\n94:     SessionID      string\n95:     BaseCommit     string\n96:     WorktreeID     string   // Internal git worktree identifier (empty for main)\n97:     ModifiedFiles  []string\n98:     NewFiles       []string\n99:     DeletedFiles   []string\n100:     MetadataDir    string   // Relative path to metadata directory\n101:     MetadataDirAbs string   // Absolute path\n102:     CommitMessage  string\n103:     // ...\n104: }\n105: \n106: type WriteCommittedOptions struct {\n107:     CheckpointID id.CheckpointID\n108:     SessionID    string\n109:     Strategy     string\n110:     Branch       string\n111:     Transcript   []byte\n112:     Prompts      []string\n113:     Context      []byte\n114:     FilesTouched []string\n115:     TokenUsage   *agent.TokenUsage\n116:     // ...\n117: }\n118: ```\n119: \n120: Token usage is defined in `agent/types.go`:\n121: \n122: ```go\n123: type TokenUsage struct {\n124:     InputTokens         int         `json:\"input_tokens\"`\n125:     CacheCreationTokens int         `json:\"cache_creation_tokens\"`\n126:     CacheReadTokens     int         `json:\"cache_read_tokens\"`\n127:     OutputTokens        int         `json:\"output_tokens\"`\n128:     APICallCount        int         `json:\"api_call_count\"`\n129:     SubagentTokens      *TokenUsage `json:\"subagent_tokens,omitempty\"`\n130: }\n131: ```\n132: \n133: ### Strategy-Level Operations\n134: \n135: Strategies compose low-level primitives into higher-level workflows.\n136: \n137: **Manual-commit** has condensation logic:\n138: \n139: ```go\n140: // CondenseSession reads accumulated temporary state and writes a committed checkpoint.\n141: func (s *ManualCommitStrategy) CondenseSession(\n142:     repo *git.Repository,\n143:     checkpointID id.CheckpointID,\n144:     state *SessionState,\n145: ) (*CondenseResult, error)\n146: ```\n147: \n148: ## Storage\n149: \n150: | Type | Location | Contents |\n151: |------|----------|----------|\n152: | Session State | `.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` | Active session tracking |\n153: | Temporary | `entire/<commit[:7]>-<worktreeHash[:6]>` branch | Full state (code + metadata) |\n154: | Committed | `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch (sharded) | Metadata + commit reference |\n155: \n156: ### Session State\n157: \n158: Location: `.git/entire-sessions/<session-id>.json`\n159: \n160: Stored in git common dir (shared across worktrees). Tracks active session info.\n161: \n162: ### Temporary Checkpoints\n163: \n164: Branch: `entire/<commit[:7]>-<worktreeHash[:6]>`\n165: \n166: Contains full worktree snapshot plus metadata overlay. **Multiple concurrent sessions** can share the same shadow branch - their checkpoints interleave:\n167: \n168: ```\n169: <worktree files...>\n170: .entire/metadata/<session-id-1>/\n171: ├── full.jsonl           # Session 1 transcript\n172: ├── prompt.txt           # Checkpoint-scoped user prompts\n173: └── tasks/<tool-use-id>/ # Task checkpoints\n174: .entire/metadata/<session-id-2>/\n175: ├── full.jsonl           # Session 2 transcript (concurrent)\n176: ├── ...\n177: ```\n178: \n179: Tied to a base commit. Condensed to committed on user commit.\n180: \n181: **Shadow branch lifecycle:**\n182: - Created on first checkpoint for a base commit\n183: - Migrated automatically if base commit changes (stash → pull → apply scenario)\n184: - Deleted after condensation to `entire/checkpoints/v1`\n185: - Reset if orphaned (no session state file exists)\n186: \n187: ### Committed Checkpoints\n188: \n189: Branch: `entire/checkpoints/v1`\n190: \n191: Metadata only, sharded by checkpoint ID. Supports **multiple sessions per checkpoint**:\n192: \n193: ```\n194: <id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/\n195: ├── metadata.json        # CheckpointSummary (aggregated stats)\n196: ├── 0/                   # First session (0-based indexing)\n197: │   ├── metadata.json    # Session-specific CommittedMetadata\n198: │   ├── full.jsonl\n199: │   ├── prompt.txt       # Checkpoint-scoped user prompts\n200: │   └── content_hash.txt\n201: ├── 1/                   # Second session\n202: │   ├── metadata.json\n203: │   ├── full.jsonl\n204: │   └── ...\n205: └── 2/                   # Third session...\n206: ```\n207: \n208: **Root-level metadata.json (`CheckpointSummary`):**\n209: ```json\n210: {\n211:   \"checkpoint_id\": \"abc123def456\",\n212:   \"strategy\": \"manual-commit\",\n213:   \"branch\": \"main\",\n214:   \"checkpoints_count\": 3,\n215:   \"files_touched\": [\"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"],\n216:   \"sessions\": [\n217:     {\n218:       \"metadata\": \"/ab/c123def456/0/metadata.json\",\n219:       \"transcript\": \"/ab/c123def456/0/full.jsonl\",\n220:       \"content_hash\": \"/ab/c123def456/0/content_hash.txt\",\n221:       \"prompt\": \"/ab/c123def456/0/prompt.txt\"\n222:     }\n223:   ],\n224:   \"token_usage\": {\n225:     \"input_tokens\": 1500,\n226:     \"cache_creation_tokens\": 200,\n227:     \"cache_read_tokens\": 800,\n228:     \"output_tokens\": 500,\n229:     \"api_call_count\": 3\n230:   }\n231: }\n232: ```\n233: \n234: When condensing multiple concurrent sessions:\n235: - All sessions are stored in numbered subdirectories using 0-based indexing (`0/`, `1/`, `2/`, ...)\n236: - Each `session_id` is assigned a stable index; subsequent writes for the same session reuse the same numbered folder\n237: - New `session_id` values are appended at the next index, so higher-numbered folders correspond to more recently introduced sessions, not necessarily the chronologically latest activity\n238: - `sessions` array in `CheckpointSummary` maps each session to its file paths\n239: - `files_touched` is merged from all sessions\n240: \n241: ### Checkpoint ID Linking\n242: \n243: The checkpoint ID is the **stable identifier** that links user commits to metadata across branches.\n244: \n245: **Format:** 12-hex-character random ID (e.g., `a3b2c4d5e6f7`)\n246: \n247: **Generation:**\n248: - Generated during condensation (post-commit hook)\n249: \n250: **Usage:**\n251: \n252: 1. **User commit trailer**:\n253:    - `Entire-Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7` added to user's commit message\n254:    - Added by `prepare-commit-msg` hook (user can remove)\n255: \n256: 2. **Directory sharding** on `entire/checkpoints/v1`:\n257:    - Path: `<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/` (e.g., `a3/b2c4d5e6f7/`)\n258:    - First 2 chars = shard (256 possible shards)\n259:    - Remaining 10 chars = directory name\n260: \n261: 3. **Commit subject** on `entire/checkpoints/v1`:\n262:    - Format: `Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7`\n263:    - Makes `git log entire/checkpoints/v1` readable\n264: \n265: **Bidirectional Lookup:**\n266: \n267: ```\n268: User commit → Metadata:\n269:   1. Extract \"Entire-Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7\" from commit message\n270:   2. Read entire/checkpoints/v1 tree at a3/b2c4d5e6f7/\n271: \n272: Metadata → User commits:\n273:   Given checkpoint ID a3b2c4d5e6f7\n274:   → Search branch history for commits with \"Entire-Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7\"\n275: ```\n276: \n277: Note: Commit subjects on `entire/checkpoints/v1` (e.g., `Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7`)\n278: are for human readability in `git log` only. The CLI always reads from the tree at HEAD.\n279: \n280: **Example Flow:**\n281: \n282: ```\n283:                     User creates commit\n284:                            ↓\n285:            prepare-commit-msg hook adds trailer\n286:                            ↓\n287: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n288: │ Commit on main branch:                           │\n289: │   \"Implement login feature                       │\n290: │                                                   │\n291: │   Entire-Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7\"               │\n292: └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n293:                            ↓\n294:                   post-commit hook runs\n295:                            ↓\n296:           Condense shadow → entire/checkpoints/v1\n297:                            ↓\n298: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n299: │ Commit on entire/checkpoints/v1:                 │\n300: │   Subject: \"Checkpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7\"            │\n301: │                                                   │\n302: │   Tree: a3/b2c4d5e6f7/                           │\n303: │     ├── metadata.json                            │\n304: │     │   (checkpoint_id: \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\")          │\n305: │     ├── 0/                                       │\n306: │     │   ├── full.jsonl                           │\n307: │     │   └── prompt.txt                           │\n308: │     └── ...                                      │\n309: │                                                   │\n310: │   Trailers:                                      │\n311: │     Entire-Session: 2026-01-20-uuid              │\n312: │     Entire-Strategy: manual-commit               │\n313: └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n314: ```\n315: \n316: The checkpoint ID creates a **bidirectional link**: user commits can find their metadata, and metadata can find the commits that reference it.\n317: \n318: ### Package Structure\n319: \n320: ```\n321: strategy/\n322: ├── session.go           # Session and Checkpoint types, ListSessions(), GetSession()\n323: \n324: session/\n325: ├── state.go             # Active session state (StateStore, .git/entire-sessions/)\n326: ├── phase.go             # Session phase state machine (ACTIVE, IDLE, ENDED, etc.)\n327: \n328: checkpoint/\n329: ├── checkpoint.go        # checkpoint.Type, checkpoint.Store interface, CheckpointSummary, etc.\n330: ├── store.go             # GitStore implementation\n331: ├── temporary.go         # Shadow branch storage\n332: ├── committed.go         # Metadata branch storage\n333: ├── id/                  # CheckpointID type and generation\n334: │   └── id.go\n335: ```\n336: \n337: Strategies use `checkpoint.Store` primitives - storage details are encapsulated.\n338: \n339: ## Strategy Role\n340: \n341: Strategies determine checkpoint timing and type:\n342: \n343: | Event | Checkpoint Type |\n344: |-------|----------------|\n345: | On Save | Temporary |\n346: | On Task Complete | Temporary |\n347: | On User Commit | Condense → Committed |\n348: \n349: ## Rewind\n350: \n351: Each `RewindPoint` includes `SessionID` and `SessionPrompt` to help identify which checkpoint belongs to which session when multiple sessions are interleaved.\n352: \n353: ## Concurrent Sessions\n354: \n355: Multiple AI sessions can run concurrently on the same base commit:\n356: \n357: 1. **Warning on start** - When a second session starts while another has uncommitted checkpoints, a warning is shown\n358: 2. **Both proceed** - User can continue; checkpoints interleave on the same shadow branch\n359: 3. **Identification** - Each checkpoint is tagged with its session ID; rewind UI shows session prompt\n360: 4. **Condensation** - On commit, all sessions are condensed together with archived subfolders\n361: \n362: ### Conflict Handling\n363: \n364: | Scenario | Behavior |\n365: |----------|----------|\n366: | Concurrent sessions (same worktree) | Warning shown, both proceed |\n367: | Orphaned shadow branch (no state file) | Branch reset, new session proceeds |\n368: | Cross-worktree conflict (state file exists) | `SessionIDConflictError` returned |\n369: \n370: ### Shadow Branch Migration\n371: \n372: If user does stash → pull → apply (HEAD changes without commit):\n373: - Detection: base commit changed AND old shadow branch still exists\n374: - Action: branch renamed from `entire/<old-commit[:7]>-<worktreeHash[:6]>` to `entire/<new-commit[:7]>-<worktreeHash[:6]>`\n375: - Result: session continues with checkpoints preserved\n376: \n377: ---\n378: \n379: ## Appendix: Legacy Names\n380: \n381: | Current | Legacy |\n382: |---------|--------|\n383: | Manual-commit | Shadow |\n\n(End of file - total 383 lines)\n</content>",
