            "output": "<path>/Users/aasheesh/Documents/webdev/os/cli/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # External Agent Plugin Protocol\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: The Entire CLI supports external agent plugins — standalone binaries that implement the Agent interface via a subcommand-based protocol over stdin/stdout. This allows third-party agents to integrate with the CLI without modifying the main repository.\n6: \n7: ## Discovery\n8: \n9: The CLI discovers external agents by scanning `$PATH` for executables matching the pattern `entire-agent-<name>`. For example, `entire-agent-cursor` would register as the \"cursor\" agent.\n10: \n11: - Binaries whose `<name>` conflicts with an already-registered built-in agent are skipped.\n12: - Discovery runs once during CLI initialization (before building the hooks command tree).\n13: - The binary must be executable and respond to the `info` subcommand.\n14: \n15: ## Environment\n16: \n17: Every subcommand invocation sets:\n18: \n19: | Variable | Description |\n20: |---|---|\n21: | `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` | Absolute path to the git repository root |\n22: | `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` | Protocol version (`1`) |\n23: \n24: The working directory is set to the repository root.\n25: \n26: ## Communication Model\n27: \n28: - **Subcommand-based:** Each Agent interface method maps to a CLI subcommand.\n29: - **JSON over stdin/stdout:** Structured data uses JSON. Transcripts use raw bytes.\n30: - **Stateless:** Each invocation is independent — no persistent connection.\n31: - **Exit codes:** `0` = success, non-zero = error. Error messages go to stderr.\n32: \n33: ## Subcommands\n34: \n35: ### Always Required\n36: \n37: #### `info`\n38: \n39: Returns agent metadata and declared capabilities.\n40: \n41: **Arguments:** None\n42: \n43: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n44: \n45: ```json\n46: {\n47:   \"protocol_version\": 1,\n48:   \"name\": \"cursor\",\n49:   \"type\": \"Cursor\",\n50:   \"description\": \"Cursor - AI-powered code editor\",\n51:   \"is_preview\": true,\n52:   \"protected_dirs\": [\".cursor\"],\n53:   \"hook_names\": [\"session-start\", \"session-end\", \"stop\"],\n54:   \"capabilities\": {\n55:     \"hooks\": true,\n56:     \"transcript_analyzer\": true,\n57:     \"compact_transcript\": true,\n58:     \"transcript_preparer\": false,\n59:     \"token_calculator\": false,\n60:     \"text_generator\": false,\n61:     \"hook_response_writer\": false,\n62:     \"subagent_aware_extractor\": false\n63:   }\n64: }\n65: ```\n66: \n67: The `capabilities` object determines which optional subcommands the CLI will call. If a capability is `false` or missing, the CLI will never invoke the corresponding subcommands.\n68: \n69: #### `detect`\n70: \n71: Checks whether the agent is present/usable in the current environment.\n72: \n73: **Arguments:** None\n74: \n75: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n76: \n77: ```json\n78: {\"present\": true}\n79: ```\n80: \n81: #### `get-session-id`\n82: \n83: Extracts the session ID from a hook input event.\n84: \n85: **Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n86: \n87: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n88: \n89: ```json\n90: {\"session_id\": \"abc123\"}\n91: ```\n92: \n93: #### `get-session-dir --repo-path <path>`\n94: \n95: Returns the directory where agent sessions are stored.\n96: \n97: **Arguments:**\n98: - `--repo-path` — Absolute path to the repository\n99: \n100: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n101: \n102: ```json\n103: {\"session_dir\": \"/path/to/sessions\"}\n104: ```\n105: \n106: #### `resolve-session-file --session-dir <dir> --session-id <id>`\n107: \n108: Resolves the session file path from a session directory and ID.\n109: \n110: **Arguments:**\n111: - `--session-dir` — Session directory path\n112: - `--session-id` — Session identifier\n113: \n114: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n115: \n116: ```json\n117: {\"session_file\": \"/path/to/session/file.jsonl\"}\n118: ```\n119: \n120: #### `read-session`\n121: \n122: Reads session data from a hook input event.\n123: \n124: **Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n125: \n126: **Output (stdout):** JSON — [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n127: \n128: ```json\n129: {\n130:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n131:   \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n132:   \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n133:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/file.jsonl\",\n134:   \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n135:   \"native_data\": null,\n136:   \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n137:   \"new_files\": [],\n138:   \"deleted_files\": []\n139: }\n140: ```\n141: \n142: #### `write-session`\n143: \n144: Writes/updates session data.\n145: \n146: **Input (stdin):** JSON — the [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n147: \n148: **Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n149: \n150: #### `read-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n151: \n152: Reads a transcript file and returns its raw bytes.\n153: \n154: **Arguments:**\n155: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n156: \n157: **Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n158: \n159: #### `chunk-transcript --max-size <n>`\n160: \n161: Splits a transcript into chunks for storage.\n162: \n163: **Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n164: \n165: **Arguments:**\n166: - `--max-size` — Maximum chunk size in bytes\n167: \n168: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n169: \n170: ```json\n171: {\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n172: ```\n173: \n174: #### `reassemble-transcript`\n175: \n176: Reassembles transcript chunks back into a full transcript.\n177: \n178: **Input (stdin):** JSON\n179: \n180: ```json\n181: {\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n182: ```\n183: \n184: **Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n185: \n186: #### `format-resume-command --session-id <id>`\n187: \n188: Returns the command a user can run to resume a session.\n189: \n190: **Arguments:**\n191: - `--session-id` — Session identifier\n192: \n193: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n194: \n195: ```json\n196: {\"command\": \"cursor --resume abc123\"}\n197: ```\n198: \n199: ### Capability: `hooks`\n200: \n201: These subcommands are required when `capabilities.hooks` is `true`.\n202: \n203: #### `parse-hook --hook <name>`\n204: \n205: Parses a raw agent hook payload into a structured event.\n206: \n207: **Arguments:**\n208: - `--hook` — Hook name (e.g., \"stop\", \"session-start\")\n209: \n210: **Input (stdin):** Raw agent hook payload bytes.\n211: \n212: **Output (stdout):** JSON — the parsed [Event object](#event-object), or `null` if the payload is not relevant.\n213: \n214: #### `install-hooks [--local-dev] [--force]`\n215: \n216: Installs agent hooks for Entire integration.\n217: \n218: **Arguments:**\n219: - `--local-dev` — Use local development binary path (optional)\n220: - `--force` — Overwrite existing hooks (optional)\n221: \n222: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n223: \n224: ```json\n225: {\"hooks_installed\": 3}\n226: ```\n227: \n228: #### `uninstall-hooks`\n229: \n230: Removes installed agent hooks.\n231: \n232: **Arguments:** None\n233: \n234: **Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n235: \n236: #### `are-hooks-installed`\n237: \n238: Checks whether hooks are currently installed.\n239: \n240: **Arguments:** None\n241: \n242: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n243: \n244: ```json\n245: {\"installed\": true}\n246: ```\n247: \n248: ### Capability: `transcript_analyzer`\n249: \n250: Required when `capabilities.transcript_analyzer` is `true`.\n251: \n252: #### `get-transcript-position --path <path>`\n253: \n254: Returns the current byte position/size of a transcript file.\n255: \n256: **Arguments:**\n257: - `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n258: \n259: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n260: \n261: ```json\n262: {\"position\": 12345}\n263: ```\n264: \n265: #### `extract-modified-files --path <path> --offset <n>`\n266: \n267: Extracts the list of files modified by the agent from a transcript.\n268: \n269: **Arguments:**\n270: - `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n271: - `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n272: \n273: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n274: \n275: ```json\n276: {\"files\": [\"path/to/file1.go\", \"path/to/file2.go\"], \"current_position\": 12345}\n277: ```\n278: \n279: The `current_position` field returns the transcript position after extraction, allowing the caller to resume from that point on subsequent calls.\n280: \n281: #### `extract-prompts --session-ref <path> --offset <n>`\n282: \n283: Extracts user prompts from a transcript.\n284: \n285: **Arguments:**\n286: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n287: - `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n288: \n289: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n290: \n291: ```json\n292: {\"prompts\": [\"first prompt text\", \"second prompt text\"]}\n293: ```\n294: \n295: #### `extract-summary --session-ref <path>`\n296: \n297: Extracts an AI-generated summary from a transcript.\n298: \n299: **Arguments:**\n300: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n301: \n302: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n303: \n304: ```json\n305: {\"summary\": \"Summary text here\", \"has_summary\": true}\n306: ```\n307: \n308: ### Capability: `transcript_preparer`\n309: \n310: Required when `capabilities.transcript_preparer` is `true`.\n311: \n312: #### `prepare-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n313: \n314: Prepares/processes a transcript file (e.g., converting from raw format).\n315: \n316: **Arguments:**\n317: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n318: \n319: **Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n320: \n321: ### Capability: `compact_transcript`\n322: \n323: Required when `capabilities.compact_transcript` is `true`.\n324: \n325: #### `compact-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n326: \n327: Builds a compact transcript representation for checkpoints v2.\n328: \n329: **Arguments:**\n330: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n331: \n332: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n333: \n334: ```json\n335: {\n336:   \"transcript\": \"eyJ0eXBlIjoiLi4uIn0K\",\n337:   \"assets\": [\n338:     {\n339:       \"name\": \"image-1.png\",\n340:       \"media_type\": \"image/png\",\n341:       \"data\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAA...\"\n342:     }\n343:   ]\n344: }\n345: ```\n346: \n347: The `transcript` field is required and must contain base64-encoded `transcript.jsonl` bytes.\n348: \n349: Those bytes must be the complete cumulative compact **Entire Transcript Format** JSONL for the session up to the current point in time (not a delta/scoped slice since the previous checkpoint).\n350: \n351: The CLI writes these bytes byte-for-byte as the full `transcript.jsonl` file for the checkpoint, so external agents must always return the entire compact transcript accumulated so far.\n352: \n353: Those bytes must satisfy the checkpoints v2 format requirements:\n354: \n355: - UTF-8 JSONL, written byte-for-byte by the CLI to `transcript.jsonl`\n356: - Newline-terminated JSONL: each record must end with `\\n`, including the final record\n357: - Every line includes format metadata (`v`, `agent`, `cli_version`) alongside the entry data\n358: - Supported top-level entry types are currently:\n359:   - `user`\n360:   - `assistant`\n361: \n362: `user` entries use `content` as an array of user blocks, typically text and optionally images:\n363: \n364: ```json\n365: {\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"user\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Fix the login bug\"}]}\n366: ```\n367: \n368: `assistant` entries use `content` as either a string or an array of assistant blocks. They may optionally include `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` fields for token usage tracking. The structured array form supports at least:\n369: \n370: - `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"...\"}`\n371: - `{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\",\"input\":{...}}`\n372: \n373: Tool output is represented inline on the preceding `tool_use` block via an optional `result` object (there is no separate top-level `user_tool_result` entry):\n374: \n375: - `\"result\": {\"output\":\"...\",\"status\":\"success|error\", ...}`\n376: \n377: Examples:\n378: \n379: ```json\n380: {\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"user\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Fix the login bug\"}]}\n381: {\"v\":1,\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"cli_version\":\"0.42.0\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"ts\":\"2026-01-13T12:00:02Z\",\"id\":\"msg_123\",\"input_tokens\":150,\"output_tokens\":42,\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I updated the file.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_123\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"src/main.go\"},\"result\":{\"output\":\"package main\",\"status\":\"success\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"src/main.go\",\"numLines\":1}}}]}\n382: ```\n383: \n384: For complete examples of the expected output format, see the [compact transcript test fixtures](../../cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/testdata/).\n385: \n386: The compact transcript should exclude agent-native envelope/progress/system noise and retain only the normalized content needed by Entire's checkpoint readers.\n387: \n388: The optional `assets` field is reserved for externalized checkpoint assets. Each asset object contains:\n389: \n390: | Field | Type | Description |\n391: |---|---|---|\n392: | `name` | string | Asset filename |\n393: | `media_type` | string | MIME type for the asset |\n394: | `data` | string | Base64-encoded asset bytes |\n395: \n396: Current CLI behavior:\n397: - If `compact_transcript` is missing or `false`, the CLI will skip compact transcript generation for that external agent, fall back to raw transcript storage, and log a warning.\n398: - If `compact-transcript` fails or returns invalid output, the CLI will also fall back to raw transcript storage and log a warning.\n399: - The CLI normalizes `transcript` bytes by appending a trailing newline when missing, and treats whitespace-only transcript output as invalid.\n400: - If `assets` are returned, the CLI accepts them in the protocol shape