\"}\n459: ```\n460: \n461: ### Capability: `hook_response_writer`\n462: \n463: Required when `capabilities.hook_response_writer` is `true`.\n464: \n465: #### `write-hook-response --message <message>`\n466: \n467: Writes a message in the agent's native hook response format.\n468: \n469: **Arguments:**\n470: - `--message` — Message to write\n471: \n472: **Output (stdout):** Agent-native format bytes (e.g., JSONL for Claude Code).\n473: \n474: ### Capability: `subagent_aware_extractor`\n475: \n476: Required when `capabilities.subagent_aware_extractor` is `true`.\n477: \n478: #### `extract-all-modified-files --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n479: \n480: Extracts modified files from both the main transcript and any subagent transcripts.\n481: \n482: **Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n483: \n484: **Arguments:**\n485: - `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n486: - `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n487: \n488: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n489: \n490: ```json\n491: {\"files\": [\"file1.go\", \"file2.go\"]}\n492: ```\n493: \n494: #### `calculate-total-tokens --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n495: \n496: Calculates total token usage across main transcript and subagent transcripts.\n497: \n498: **Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n499: \n500: **Arguments:**\n501: - `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n502: - `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n503: \n504: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n505: \n506: ```json\n507: {\n508:   \"input_tokens\": 5000,\n509:   \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n510:   \"cache_read_tokens\": 1000,\n511:   \"output_tokens\": 2000,\n512:   \"api_call_count\": 8,\n513:   \"subagent_tokens\": {\n514:     \"input_tokens\": 2000,\n515:     \"output_tokens\": 800\n516:   }\n517: }\n518: ```\n519: \n520: Same token usage format as `calculate-tokens`. The `subagent_tokens` field aggregates usage from all subagents.\n521: \n522: ## Shared Object Definitions\n523: \n524: ### HookInput Object\n525: \n526: The HookInput object is passed via stdin to `get-session-id` and `read-session`.\n527: \n528: ```json\n529: {\n530:   \"hook_type\": \"stop\",\n531:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n532:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n533:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n534:   \"user_prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n535:   \"tool_name\": \"Write\",\n536:   \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_abc123\",\n537:   \"tool_input\": {\"path\": \"/src/main.go\"},\n538:   \"raw_data\": {\"custom_field\": \"value\"}\n539: }\n540: ```\n541: \n542: | Field | Type | Description |\n543: |---|---|---|\n544: | `hook_type` | string | Hook type: `session_start`, `session_end`, `user_prompt_submit`, `stop`, `pre_tool_use`, `post_tool_use` |\n545: | `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n546: | `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific session reference (typically a file path) |\n547: | `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp |\n548: | `user_prompt` | string | User's prompt text (from `user_prompt_submit` hooks). Optional. |\n549: | `tool_name` | string | Tool name (from `pre_tool_use`/`post_tool_use` hooks). Optional. |\n550: | `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID. Optional. |\n551: | `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON. Optional. |\n552: | `raw_data` | object | Agent-specific data for extension. Optional. |\n553: \n554: ### AgentSession Object\n555: \n556: Used as input to `write-session` and output from `read-session`.\n557: \n558: ```json\n559: {\n560:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n561:   \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n562:   \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n563:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n564:   \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n565:   \"native_data\": null,\n566:   \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n567:   \"new_files\": [\"src/new_file.go\"],\n568:   \"deleted_files\": []\n569: }\n570: ```\n571: \n572: | Field | Type | Description |\n573: |---|---|---|\n574: | `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n575: | `agent_name` | string | Agent registry name |\n576: | `repo_path` | string | Absolute path to the repository |\n577: | `session_ref` | string | Path/reference to session in agent's storage |\n578: | `start_time` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp of session start |\n579: | `native_data` | bytes/null | Session content in agent's native format (opaque to CLI) |\n580: | `modified_files` | string[] | Files modified during the session |\n581: | `new_files` | string[] | Files created during the session |\n582: | `deleted_files` | string[] | Files deleted during the session |\n583: \n584: ### Event Object\n585: \n586: Returned by `parse-hook`. Represents a normalized lifecycle event.\n587: \n588: ```json\n589: {\n590:   \"type\": 3,\n591:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n592:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n593:   \"prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n594:   \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n595:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\"\n596: }\n597: ```\n598: \n599: | Field | Type | Description |\n600: |---|---|---|\n601: | `type` | int | **Required.** Event type (see table below) |\n602: | `session_id` | string | **Required.** Agent session identifier |\n603: | `previous_session_id` | string | Non-empty when this event represents a session continuation/handoff. Optional. |\n604: | `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific transcript reference. Optional. |\n605: | `prompt` | string | User's prompt text (on `TurnStart` events). Optional. |\n606: | `model` | string | LLM model identifier. Optional. |\n607: | `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp. Optional. |\n608: | `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n609: | `subagent_id` | string | Subagent instance ID (for `SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n610: | `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON (for subagent type/description extraction). Optional. |\n611: | `subagent_type` | string | Kind of subagent (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n612: | `task_description` | string | Subagent task description. Optional. |\n613: | `response_message` | string | Message to display to the user via the agent. Optional. |\n614: | `metadata` | object | Agent-specific state preserved across events. Optional. |\n615: \n616: **Event types:**\n617: \n618: | Value | Name | Description |\n619: |---|---|---|\n620: | 1 | SessionStart | Agent session has begun |\n621: | 2 | TurnStart | User submitted a prompt, agent is about to work |\n622: | 3 | TurnEnd | Agent finished responding to a prompt |\n623: | 4 | Compaction | Agent is compressing its context window (triggers save + offset reset) |\n624: | 5 | SessionEnd | Session has been terminated |\n625: | 6 | SubagentStart | A subagent (task) has been spawned |\n626: | 7 | SubagentEnd | A subagent (task) has completed |\n627: \n628: ## Error Handling\n629: \n630: - Exit code `0` indicates success.\n631: - Any non-zero exit code indicates an error.\n632: - Error messages should be written to stderr.\n633: - The CLI captures stderr and wraps it in a Go error.\n634: - If the binary is not found in PATH, the agent is simply not registered.\n635: - If `info` fails or returns invalid JSON, the binary is skipped during discovery.\n636: \n637: ## Versioning\n638: \n639: The protocol version is declared in the `info` response (`protocol_version` field) and set via `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` environment variable. The CLI checks that the binary's protocol version matches its expected version before registering the agent.\n640: \n641: Future protocol versions may add new subcommands or capabilities. Existing subcommands will maintain backwards compatibility within a major version.\n\n(End of file - total 641 lines)\n</content>",
