          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I understand the full picture. Let me give you a **concrete implementation plan** with specific features to build:\n\n---\n\n## Features to Implement (Based on Roadmap)\n\n### 1. **Knowledge Base / Cross-Session Learning** \n*Matches Antigravity's \"Agents learn patterns from past tasks\"*\n\n**What to build:** Store learned patterns from checkpoints that agents can query\n\n**Files to create:**\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/knowledge/\n├── knowledge.go        # Knowledge base interface\n├── patterns.go        # Pattern extraction from checkpoints  \n├── query.go           # Query patterns for new sessions\n└── store.go           # Git-based pattern storage\n```\n\n**Usage:** Agents can query \"what patterns worked for similar tasks?\" before starting work\n\n**Example command:**\n```bash\nentire knowledge add --pattern \"auth error handling\" --from-checkpoint <id>\nentire knowledge query \"fix login bug\"  # returns similar successful patterns\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Searchable Prompts Enhancement**\n*Matches Roadmap: \"surfacing the prompt that introduced a workaround\"*\n\n**What to build:** Extend `entire search` to index and search prompts (not just code)\n\n**Files to modify:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search/search.go` - Add prompt index support\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search/prompts.go` - New prompt search specific code\n\n**New command:**\n```bash\nentire search --prompts \"fix auth bug\"    # Search only prompts\nentire search --prompts \"implement login\" --files   # Search both\n```\n\n**Current gap:** `entire search` only searches code/diffs, not prompts/transcripts\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Intent Review Enhancement**\n*Matches Roadmap: \"replacing code reviews with intent reviews\"*\n\n**What to build:** Pre-commit \"intent summary\" that shows prompt before diff\n\n**Files to modify:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/intent.go` - New intent review module\n- Add `entire intent` command\n\n**New workflow:**\n```\nBefore commit:\n1. Show: \"You asked: fix login bug\"\n2. Show: \"Files changed: src/auth.go, tests/auth_test.go\"  \n3. Show: \"This matches checkpoint pattern from <date>\"\n4. Human approves or modifies intent\n```\n\n**Files to create:**\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/intent/\n├── intent.go           # Main intent command\n├── precommit.go        # Pre-commit intent capture\n└── diff.go            # Intent vs diff comparison\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Checkpoint Remote Enhancement**  \n*Better team collaboration*\n\n**What to build:** Push checkpoints to team-shared remote with access controls\n\n**Files to modify:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/remote/remote.go` - Add team remote support\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` - Add team settings\n\n**New settings:**\n```json\n{\n  \"team_remote\": {\n    \"provider\": \"github\",\n    \"repo\": \"myorg/checkpoints\",\n    \"visibility\": \"private\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quickest Win: Intent Review\n\nLet me show you the implementation for **Intent Review** - it's the most aligned with their roadmap:\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/intent/intent.go - New file\n\npackage intent\n\nimport (\n    \"context\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"strings\"\n\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint\"\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/summarize\"\n)\n\ntype IntentSummary struct {\n    Prompt      string\n    Checkpoint  checkpointID\n    Similarity  float64\n    Files       []string\n    Model       string\n    Agent       string\n}\n\n// ComputeIntent generates an intent summary for a commit\nfunc ComputeIntent(ctx context.Context, files []string) (*IntentSummary, error) {\n    // 1. Get most recent checkpoint\n    // 2. Extract prompt from transcript\n    // 3. Find similar historical intents\n    // 4. Return intent summary\n}\n\n// formatIntentSummary renders the intent for human review\nfunc formatIntentSummary(i *IntentSummary) string {\n    return fmt.Sprintf(`\nIntent: %s\n\nCheckpoint: %s\nAgent: %s (%s)\nFiles: %s\n\nSimilar patterns found: %.0f%% match\n`, i.Prompt, i.Checkpoint, i.Agent, i.Model, \n   strings.Join(i.Files, \", \"), i.Similarity * 100)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Want me to implement any of these?\n\nI can start with the **quickest-to-ship** feature that will get you a PR merged:\n\n1. **Intent Review** (Most aligned with roadmap) - 2-3 days\n2. **Searchable Prompts** (Extends existing `search`) - 3-4 days  \n3. **Knowledge Base** (New package) - 5-7 days\n\nWhich one should I start implementing? Or do you want me to investigate a different gap?",
