              "patch": "Index: docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md\n===================================================================\n--- docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md\t\n+++ docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md\t\n@@ -0,0 +1,461 @@\n+# Feature Proposal: Searchable Prompts & Intent Review CLI\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+**Goal:** Implement CLI commands that let users search their checkpoint history by *what they asked the agent*, not just what code changed.\n+\n+**Problem:** Developers can search code (git blame, grep) but cannot search *intent* - the prompts that led to decisions. \"Why did we use this library?\" → need to find the prompt, not the code.\n+\n+**Roadmap Alignment:** Entire explicitly listed \"searchable prompts\" and \"intent review\" as future goals (March 2026 roadmap).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 1: Current Product State\n+\n+### What's Already Built\n+\n+#### Checkpoint System\n+- Captures: transcripts, prompts, files touched, token usage, timestamps\n+- Storage: Git branch (`entire/checkpoints/v1`)\n+- Metadata structure (from `checkpoint.go`):\n+  ```go\n+  type CheckpointSummary struct {\n+      CheckpointID  string\n+      FilesTouched []string\n+      Sessions      []SessionInfo\n+      // NO PROMPT FIELD at summary level\n+  }\n+  \n+  type SessionContent struct {\n+      Transcript   []byte\n+      Prompts      []string  // Stored but not indexed\n+      Metadata     CommittedMetadata\n+  }\n+  \n+  type CommittedMetadata struct {\n+      Kind        string   // \"session\" | \"agent_review\"\n+      ReviewSkills []string\n+      ReviewPrompt string\n+  }\n+  ```\n+\n+#### Existing Search (`entire search`)\n+- Uses external search API (entire.io service)\n+- Searches code/diffs, not prompts\n+- Requires authentication\n+- Based on hybrid semantic + keyword search\n+\n+#### Existing Review (`entire review`)\n+- Runs configured review skills against branch\n+- Multi-agent support (TUI with Bubble Tea)\n+- Review sessions tagged in checkpoints\n+- NOT \"intent-first\" - still diff-centric\n+\n+#### Skills System (New - May 2026)\n+- Agents can search their own history via skills\n+- `search` skill for agents\n+- `explain` skill for agents\n+- Cross-agent compatible\n+- **For agents, not users**\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 2: Roadmap Status\n+\n+### From March 25, 2026 Blog: \"The Entire CLI: How It Works & Where It's Headed\"\n+\n+| Feature | Status | Notes |\n+|---------|--------|-------|\n+| **Team Visibility** | Not shipped | \"Git tells you who committed. Entire shows how it was built.\" |\n+| **Searchable Prompts** | **NOT SHIPPED** | \"surfacing the prompt that introduced a workaround\" |\n+| **Audit Attribution** | Partial | Line-level attribution exists; full audit trail in progress |\n+| **Intent Review** | **NOT SHIPPED** | \"moving beyond the diff to replace code reviews with intent reviews\" |\n+\n+### From May 7, 2026 Blog: \"Bring Structure to Your Agent Workflows\"\n+- `entire labs` command for experimental workflows\n+- `entire recap` command for browsing recaps\n+- `entire review` command (skills-based)\n+- Skills system for agents to search history\n+\n+**Key Finding:** Skills are for *agents* to search. Users still cannot search prompts via CLI.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 3: The Gap\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+**User need:** \"I need to find when we decided to use Redis instead of Memcached\"\n+\n+**Current workflow:**\n+1. Grep for \"redis\" in code → finds usage, not *decision*\n+2. Git blame → shows who, not *why*\n+3. Check Slack/Notion/Google Docs → fragmented\n+4. Ask teammates → unreliable\n+\n+**With searchable prompts:**\n+```bash\n+entire prompts search \"cache\"\n+# → \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached?\" - 2026-03-15\n+# → \"Add Redis caching for session store\" - 2026-04-02\n+```\n+\n+### User Stories\n+\n+1. **Investigate regression:** \"This auth flow is complex. Find when we discussed it.\"\n+2. **Understand decisions:** \"Why did we pick this library? What was the context?\"\n+3. **Find similar work:** \"Has anyone worked on OAuth before?\"\n+4. **Onboarding:** \"Show me how this feature was built\"\n+5. **Audit:** \"What prompts led to this security fix?\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 4: Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Option A: `entire prompts` Command (Recommended)\n+\n+**New command structure:**\n+```bash\n+entire prompts list                    # List recent prompts\n+entire prompts search <query>          # Search prompts\n+entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>   # Show prompt for checkpoint\n+entire prompts diff <checkpoint-id>   # Show prompt + diff together\n+```\n+\n+**Why Option A:**\n+- Clear, discoverable namespace\n+- Mirrors `entire checkpoint` structure\n+- Extends existing architecture\n+\n+### Option B: Extend `entire search` with `--prompts`\n+\n+```bash\n+entire search --prompts \"cache\"       # Search prompts only\n+entire search --both \"cache\"         # Search both prompts and code\n+```\n+\n+**Why not Option B:**\n+- Search already requires auth + API\n+- Prompts are local (git branch), should work offline\n+- Different use case: search vs explore\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 5: Technical Architecture\n+\n+### Data Flow\n+\n+```\n+Checkpoint Created\n+    ↓\n+Prompts Extracted from Transcript\n+    ↓\n+Stored in Git Branch\n+    ├── Prompt text (full)\n+    ├── Embedding vector (future)\n+    └── Metadata (checkpoint_id, session_id, timestamp)\n+    ↓\n+User Queries\n+    ↓\n+Local Index (SQLite) ← New component\n+    ↓\n+Results Displayed\n+```\n+\n+### Components to Build\n+\n+```\n+cmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n+├── prompts.go           # Main command group\n+├── list.go             # entire prompts list\n+├── search.go           # entire prompts search  \n+├── show.go             # entire prompts show\n+├── diff.go             # entire prompts diff (prompt + files)\n+├── indexer.go          # Build/update local prompt index\n+├── store.go            # SQLite-based prompt storage\n+├── embed.go            # (Future) Embedding generation\n+└── test/\n+    ├── prompts_test.go\n+    ├── search_test.go\n+    └── indexer_test.go\n+```\n+\n+### Data Model\n+\n+```go\n+// Local prompt store\n+type PromptStore struct {\n+    db *sql.DB\n+}\n+\n+type Prompt struct {\n+    ID            string    // UUID\n+    CheckpointID  string    // From checkpoint\n+    SessionID     string    // From session\n+    Text          string    // Full prompt text\n+    Timestamp     time.Time\n+    Agent         string    // \"Claude Code\", etc.\n+    Model         string    // \"claude-opus-4\"\n+    FilesChanged  []string // Files in this checkpoint\n+    Branch        string\n+    Author        string    // Git author\n+}\n+\n+type SearchResult struct {\n+    Prompt   Prompt\n+    Score    float64      // Similarity score\n+    Matches  []string     // Matching terms\n+    Context  string       // Surrounding context (files)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Index Strategy\n+\n+**Phase 1: Full-text search (immediate)**\n+```sql\n+CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE prompts USING fts5(\n+    text,\n+    checkpoint_id UNINDEXED,\n+    session_id UNINDEXED\n+);\n+```\n+\n+**Phase 2: Semantic search (future)**\n+- Generate embeddings from prompts\n+- Store vectors alongside text\n+- Use cosine similarity for ranking\n+- Can use local model (llama.cpp) or API\n+\n+**Phase 3: Cross-repo search (future)**\n+- Push index to checkpoint remote\n+- Search across team's history\n+- Privacy controls\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 6: Algorithms & Methods\n+\n+### Search Algorithm Comparison\n+\n+| Algorithm | Pros | Cons | Recommendation |\n+|-----------|------|------|----------------|\n+| **BM25** | Fast, good for keyword | No semantic understanding | Phase 1 fallback |\n+| **TF-IDF** | Simple, interpretable | Ignores word order | Not recommended |\n+| **Dense Retrieval** | Semantic matching | Needs embeddings | Phase 2 |\n+| **Hybrid (BM25 + Dense)** | Best of both | Complexity | Phase 2+ |\n+\n+### Recommended Approach: TF-IDF + Trigram (Phase 1)\n+\n+```go\n+// Simple but effective for local prompts\n+// Based on PostgreSQL's pg_trgm + ts_rank pattern\n+\n+type PromptSearcher struct {\n+    db *sql.DB\n+}\n+\n+func (s *PromptSearcher) Search(query string, limit int) ([]Prompt, error) {\n+    // 1. Tokenize query\n+    tokens := tokenize(query)\n+    \n+    // 2. Build weighted SQL query\n+    // - Exact phrase matches: high weight\n+    // - Individual word matches: medium weight\n+    // - All tokens must match (AND semantics)\n+    \n+    sql := `\n+        SELECT p.*, \n+            ts_rank(to_tsvector('english', p.text), query) as rank\n+        FROM prompts p, to_tsquery('english', ?) as query\n+        WHERE to_tsvector('english', p.text) @@ query\n+        ORDER BY rank DESC\n+        LIMIT ?\n+    `\n+    \n+    return s.db.Query(sql, tokens, limit)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Semantic Search (Phase 2)\n+\n+**Option 1: Local embeddings (Privacy-first)**\n+```bash\n+# Embedding model (quantized, ~1GB)\n+sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\n+```\n+\n+**Option 2: API-based (Simpler)**\n+```bash\n+# Use existing provider\n+openai embeddings / anthropic embeddings\n+```\n+\n+**Hybrid Ranking Formula:**\n+```\n+FinalScore = α × BM25Score + (1-α) × CosineSimilarity\n+```\n+- α = 0.3 for prompts (semantic > keyword)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 7: Edge Cases\n+\n+### 1. Large Transcripts\n+- **Problem:** Single session can have 100+ prompts\n+- **Solution:** Index all prompts; show session grouping in results\n+\n+### 2. Multi-turn Context\n+- **Problem:** \"Continue\" or follow-up prompts lack full context\n+- **Solution:** Include parent prompt reference; show conversation thread\n+\n+### 3. Binary/File Prompts\n+- **Problem:** Some prompts are just \"fix tests\" with no detail\n+- **Solution:** Use checkpoint description as fallback; warn on weak prompts\n+\n+### 4. Non-English Prompts\n+- **Problem:** Tokenizers/embeddings may not handle mixed languages\n+- **Solution:** UTF-8 support; language detection; separate indexes\n+\n+### 5. Privacy/Sensitive Prompts\n+- **Problem:** Prompts may contain secrets, PII\n+- **Solution:** Re-use existing PII redaction; exclude from index option\n+\n+### 6. Offline Mode\n+- **Problem:** User disconnected from internet\n+- **Solution:** Local SQLite index works offline; cross-repo needs connectivity\n+\n+### 7. Fresh Index\n+- **Problem:** No prompts indexed yet\n+- **Solution:** Index built incrementally; initial build is background job\n+\n+### 8. Merge Conflicts\n+- **Problem:** Multiple checkpoints condensed\n+- **Solution:** Index uses checkpoint_id, not commit order; dedup by ID\n+\n+### 9. Session Resume\n+- **Problem:** Resumed sessions have different checkpoint IDs\n+- **Solution:** Link resumed sessions via PreviousSessionID\n+\n+### 10. Deleted/Pruned Checkpoints\n+- **Problem:** Checkpoint deleted, but prompt in search results\n+- **Solution:** Graceful degradation; show \"checkpoint unavailable\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 8: Intent Review (Separate Feature)\n+\n+### What Intent Review Means\n+\n+**Current:** Review code diffs\n+```\n+diff --git a/auth.go\n+- if user == nil {\n++ if user == nil || user.Expired() {\n+```\n+\n+**Intent Review:** Review what was asked\n+```\n+Prompt: \"Fix auth bug - users staying logged in after token expires\"\n+Agent: Claude Code (Sonnet 4)\n+Files: auth.go, auth_test.go\n+Context: Related to security audit #123\n+Similar: 3 previous auth-related changes\n+```\n+\n+### Implementation Options\n+\n+#### Option A: `entire review --intent` (Extends existing)\n+```bash\n+entire review --intent        # Intent-first review\n+entire review --diff         # Traditional diff review\n+entire review --both         # Both views\n+```\n+\n+#### Option B: New `entire intent` Command\n+```bash\n+entire intent show           # Show current commit's intent\n+entire intent compare        # Compare with previous\n+entire intent validate       # Check intent matches diff\n+```\n+\n+### Recommended: Option A (extend `entire review`)\n+\n+**Rationale:**\n+- Reuse existing infrastructure\n+- Skills already work with checkpoints\n+- Single command family\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 9: Related Features Comparison\n+\n+| Feature | Current | Proposed | Priority |\n+|---------|---------|----------|----------|\n+| Prompt storage | ✅ Git branch | Same | - |\n+| Prompt display | ❌ Not exposed | `entire prompts show` | P1 |\n+| Prompt search | ❌ Not built | `entire prompts search` | P1 |\n+| Semantic search | ❌ Not built | Embeddings | P2 |\n+| Intent review | ❌ Not built | `entire review --intent` | P2 |\n+| Cross-repo prompts | ❌ Not built | Remote index | P3 |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 10: Implementation Plan\n+\n+### Phase 1: Core Prompt Access (Week 1-2)\n+```\n+1. Create cmd/entire/cli/prompts/ package\n+2. Implement local SQLite index\n+3. Build `entire prompts list`\n+4. Build `entire prompts show`\n+5. Build `entire prompts search` (keyword only)\n+6. Add tests\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 2: Enhanced Search (Week 3-4)\n+```\n+7. Add TF-IDF ranking\n+8. Add file context in results\n+9. Add session threading\n+10. Performance optimization\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 3: Semantic Search (Week 5-6)\n+```\n+11. Add embedding generation\n+12. Implement hybrid search\n+13. Add privacy controls\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 4: Intent Review (Week 7-8)\n+```\n+14. Extend entire review with --intent\n+15. Add intent summary generation\n+16. Add intent vs diff comparison\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Part 11: Success Metrics\n+\n+### Quantitative\n+- Prompts indexed per day\n+- Search queries per user per week\n+- Click-through rate on search results\n+- Zero failed searches (no results)\n+\n+### Qualitative\n+- \"I found the decision I was looking for\"\n+- \"This saved me hours of investigation\"\n+- \"I can finally explain why we made this choice\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+## References\n+\n+1. [Entire Roadmap Blog](https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed)\n+2. [Skills Announcement](https://entire.io/blog/bring-your-entire-context-to-your-agents-with-skills)\n+3. [Checkpoint Scenarios](docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md)\n+4. [Agent Integration Guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md)\n+5. BM25 Algorithm: Robertson & Zaragoza (2009)\n+6. Hybrid Search: Formalizing Neural-Sparse Retrieval (Khalid et al, 2022)\n",
