              "content": "# Feature Proposal: Searchable Prompts CLI\n\n**Feature:** `entire prompts search` — Searchable prompts from checkpoint history\n**Roadmap:** https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed (March 2026)\n**Status:** Not shipped, not in progress\n**Updated:** May 2026\n\n---\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\n\n> \"We're making that answer searchable. Users will be able to surface the prompt that introduced a workaround or revisit the reasoning behind a library choice months later. The 'why' will be part of your history.\" — Entire Roadmap\n\nDevelopers can search **what changed** (git blame, grep) but cannot search **why it changed** — the prompts that led to decisions.\n\n**Example:** \"Why did we pick Redis over Memcached?\"\n- Grep for \"redis\" → finds usage, not decision\n- Git blame → shows who, not why\n- Slack/Notion/Google Docs → fragmented\n- Ask teammates → unreliable\n\n**With searchable prompts:**\n```\n$ entire prompts search \"cache decision\"\n→ \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached?\"  a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code\n→ \"Add Redis caching for session store\"       7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Roadmap Alignment\n\n| Feature | Status | Roadmap Section |\n|---------|--------|----------------|\n| **Searchable Prompts** | NOT SHIPPED | \"Search\" — surfacing the prompt that introduced a workaround |\n| Intent Review | NOT SHIPPED | \"Rethinking Code Review to Intent Review\" |\n| Team Visibility | NOT SHIPPED | \"Team Visibility\" |\n| Audit & Transparency | Partial | Line-level attribution exists |\n\n**This proposal covers only \"Searchable Prompts.\"** Intent review is a separate feature.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Current Architecture\n\n### What Already Exists\n\n```\nCheckpoint Condensation\n      ↓\nGitStore.WriteCommitted()\n      ↓\nentire/checkpoints/v1 branch\n      ↓\n<checkpoint-id[:2]>/<checkpoint-id[2:]>/\n├── metadata.json           # CheckpointSummary (no prompts)\n├── 0/                       # Session 0\n│   ├── metadata.json        # CommittedMetadata\n│   ├── full.jsonl          # Transcript\n│   └── prompt.txt           # User prompts (multi-turn, split by \"---\\n\\n\")\n├── 1/                       # Session 1 (if multi-session)\n...\n```\n\n**Key types (from `checkpoint/checkpoint.go`):**\n```go\ntype CheckpointSummary struct {\n    CheckpointID     id.CheckpointID\n    Sessions         []SessionFilePaths  // paths to session dirs\n    FilesTouched     []string\n    HasReview        bool\n}\n\ntype CommittedMetadata struct {\n    SessionID        string\n    Agent            types.AgentType\n    Model            string\n    CreatedAt        time.Time\n    CheckpointsCount int\n    Kind             string  // \"session\" | \"agent_review\"\n    ReviewSkills     []string\n    ReviewPrompt     string\n}\n\ntype SessionContent struct {\n    Transcript        []byte\n    Prompts           string  // full prompt.txt content (multi-turn)\n    Metadata          CommittedMetadata\n}\n```\n\n**Key reading methods (from `checkpoint/committed.go`):**\n- `GitStore.ListCommitted()` → scans all checkpoint dirs, reads metadata\n- `GitStore.ReadLatestSessionContent()` → reads full session content including prompts\n- `GitStore.ReadSessionContent(ctx, cpID, sessionIndex)` → reads specific session\n\n**Key reading methods (from `strategy/common.go`):**\n- `ReadLatestSessionPromptFromCommittedTree()` → reads first prompt from prompt.txt\n- `ReadAllSessionPromptsFromTree()` → reads all session prompts (multi-session)\n- `ExtractFirstPrompt()` → extracts first non-empty prompt from prompt.txt content\n\n**Sharding:** Checkpoint IDs are sharded into 256 buckets using first 2 hex chars.\nPath: `a3/b2c4d5e6f7/` (from `id.CheckpointID.Path()`)\n\n### What's Missing\n\n- **No CLI command** to search prompt text — prompts exist in git but aren't exposed\n- **No search index** — every search would need to walk all checkpoint trees\n- **No ranking** — even if you could walk, there's no relevance scoring\n- **Existing `entire search`** — searches code/diffs via external API, not prompts\n\n---\n\n## 4. Design Goals\n\n1. **Offline-first** — works without internet, no external API dependency\n2. **Git-native** — leverages existing `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch, no new storage\n3. **Zero config** — works immediately, no setup required\n4. **Incrementally updated** — index built once at condensation time\n5. **Fast queries** — sub-second search over thousands of prompts\n6. **Privacy-preserving** — PII redaction already in place, no new exposure\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Approaches\n\n### Approach A: On-Demand Git Tree Scan (No Index)\n\n**How it works:**\n- On every search, walk the entire/checkpoints/v1 tree and read all prompt.txt files\n- No persistent index, just raw git tree traversal\n\n**Pros:**\n- Zero additional storage\n- Always up-to-date (no sync needed)\n- No complexity\n\n**Cons:**\n- O(n) on number of checkpoints — slow at scale\n- Reads every blob on every query — expensive\n- No ranking — just substring match\n\n**Verdict:** Not acceptable. 1000 checkpoints = 1000 blob reads per search.\n\n---\n\n### Approach B: In-Memory Index (Built at Query Time)\n\n**How it works:**\n- On first search, read all checkpoint metadata + prompts into memory\n- Cache in process, rebuild on invalidation\n- Subsequent searches are in-memory\n\n**Pros:**\n- Fast queries after initial warm-up\n- Simple implementation\n- No disk storage\n\n**Cons:**\n- Memory grows unbounded\n- Initial warm-up slow on large repos\n- No persistence across CLI invocations\n\n**Verdict:** Not ideal but acceptable for MVP. Simple, works offline, fast enough.\n\n---\n\n### Approach C: Persistent Local Index (File-based)\n\n**How it works:**\n- Build a persistent index stored in `.entire/prompts/` (gitignored)\n- Index file stores: checkpoint ID, session ID, prompt text (truncated), timestamp, agent, files touched\n- Updated incrementally at condensation time (PostCommit hook adds new entries)\n- On search, read index file and filter/rank in-memory\n\n**Pros:**\n- Persistent across CLI invocations\n- Fast warm-up (just read index file)\n- Incremental updates (only new checkpoints added)\n- Works offline, no external deps\n\n**Cons:**\n- New file in `.entire/` (gitignored, but needs management)\n- Index file could grow large (mitigated by truncation + compression)\n- Need to handle index invalidation on branch operations\n\n**Verdict:** RECOMMENDED. Best balance of simplicity, performance, and UX.\n\n---\n\n### Approach D: SQLite FTS5 (Full-Text Search)\n\n**How it works:**\n- Store prompts in a SQLite database with FTS5 virtual table\n- Use SQLite's built-in BM25 ranking\n\n**Pros:**\n- Best-in-class full-text search\n- Handles large datasets well\n- Mature technology\n\n**Cons:**\n- **CGO dependency** — requires `gcc` to compile sqlite3, adds complexity to builds\n- Binary size increase (~2MB)\n- Not already a dependency in this project\n- Cross-platform build complexity\n\n**Verdict:** Not for Phase 1. Good future option if we want advanced ranking.\n\n---\n\n### Approach E: External Search API (Cloud)\n\n**How it works:**\n- Push prompt index to Entire's cloud service\n- Search via `entire search` command (already exists for code)\n\n**Pros:**\n- Best search quality (embeddings + BM25)\n- Cross-repo search\n\n**Cons:**\n- Requires auth + internet\n- Not offline-first\n- Not user-owned data\n\n**Verdict:** Not for this feature. `entire prompts` should be local-first.\n\n---\n\n### Chosen Approach: Approach C (Persistent Local Index)\n\n**Summary:**\n- Store index as a compressed JSON file in `.entire/prompts/index.json.gz`\n- Index built/updated at PostCommit hook (condensation time)\n- In-memory search with in-memory ranking\n- Fallback to on-demand scan if index is missing/corrupt\n\n**Why:**\n- Simple (JSON, no new deps)\n- Fast (compressed but small enough to read quickly)\n- Offline-first (no API needed)\n- Incremental (only new checkpoints added)\n- Git-native (lives in `.entire/`, gitignored)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Search Algorithm\n\n### Phase 1: Keyword Search (BM25-style)\n\n**Algorithm:** Weighted substring matching with ranking\n\n**Ranking formula:**\n```\nScore = (exact_phrase_matches * 10) + (all_words_found * 5) + (any_word_found * 1)\n```\n\nWhere:\n- **exact_phrase_matches**: Query as a phrase (all words adjacent in order)\n- **all_words_found**: Every query word appears somewhere in the prompt\n- **any_word_found**: At least one query word appears\n\n**Tokenization:**\n- Lowercase, trim\n- Split on whitespace\n- Remove common stop words: \"the\", \"a\", \"an\", \"is\", \"are\", \"was\", \"were\", \"to\", \"of\", \"in\", \"for\", \"and\", \"or\", \"but\"\n- Support quoted phrases: `\"redis cache\"` treated as exact match\n\n**Example:**\n```\nQuery: \"add redis caching\"\nPrompt: \"Add Redis caching for session store\"\n→ exact match: no (\"add redis caching\" not contiguous)\n→ all words found: yes (add, redis, caching all present)\n→ score = 5\n```\n\n**Result ordering:**\n1. Exact phrase matches (highest score)\n2. All words found\n3. Any word found\n4. Within same tier: newer checkpoints first\n\n---\n\n## 7. Data Flow\n\n### Index Build (at condensation / PostCommit hook)\n\n```\nUser commits → PostCommit hook → Strategy.Condense()\n      ↓\nWriteCommitted() writes checkpoint to entire/checkpoints/v1\n      ↓\ncondenseAndUpdateState() returns sessionData with Prompts\n      ↓\nPromptsIndexer.AddCheckpoint(cpID, sessionData)\n      ↓\nRead checkpoint metadata (Agent, Model, FilesTouched, CreatedAt, Branch)\nRead prompt.txt content (truncate to 2000 chars for index)\nWrite index entry to .entire/prompts/index.json.gz\n```\n\n**Index entry schema:**\n```go\ntype PromptIndex struct {\n    Version   int              // index format version (1)\n    UpdatedAt  time.Time        // last index update\n    Checkpoints []PromptEntry  // sorted by checkpoint ID (not time)\n}\n\ntype PromptEntry struct {\n    CheckpointID  string    // \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\"\n    SessionID     string    // \"2026-03-15-uuid\"\n    PromptText    string    // truncated to 2000 chars\n    Agent         string    // \"Claude Code\"\n    Model         string    // \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\"\n    FilesTouched  []string  // files modified\n    Branch        string    // branch name at commit time\n    CreatedAt     time.Time // checkpoint creation time\n}\n```\n\n### Query (at search command)\n\n```\nentire prompts search \"redis cache\"\n      ↓\nLoadIndex() — read .entire/prompts/index.json.gz into memory\n      ↓\nTokenizeQuery(\"redis cache\") → [\"redis\", \"cache\"]\n      ↓\nSearch(checkpoints, query) — rank all entries\n      ↓\nFormatResults() — display top 20 results with context\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Command Interface\n\n### `entire prompts search <query>`\n\n**Usage:**\n```\nentire prompts search <query>          # Search prompts\nentire prompts search \"redis cache\"    # Search for specific terms\nentire prompts search --limit 50       # Show more results\nentire prompts search --json           # JSON output\nentire prompts search --agent claude   # Filter by agent\nentire prompts search --branch feat/x  # Filter by branch\nentire prompts search --after 2026-03  # Filter by date\n```\n\n**Output format:**\n```\nSearch results for \"redis cache\" (23 found)\n\n  a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code  main\n  \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached for the caching layer?\"\n\n  7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI   feat/cache\n  \"Add Redis caching for session store to improve latency\"\n\n  f1e2d3c4b5a6  2026-04-15  Claude Code  main\n  \"Migrate in-memory cache to Redis cluster for production\"\n```\n\n**With `--json`:**\n```json\n{\n  \"query\": \"redis cache\",\n  \"total\": 23,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"checkpoint_id\": \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\",\n      \"session_id\": \"2026-03-15-uuid\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached...\",\n      \"agent\": \"Claude Code\",\n      \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-15T10:30:00Z\",\n      \"files_touched\": [\"cache/redis.go\", \"cache/memcached.go\"],\n      \"score\": 8\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### `entire prompts list`\n\n**Usage:**\n```\nentire prompts list                  # List recent prompts (last 20)\nentire prompts list --limit 50       # Show more\nentire prompts list --checkpoint abc # Show prompts for specific checkpoint\n```\n\n**Output format:**\n```\nRecent prompts (20 shown, 150 total)\n\n  a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code  main\n  \"Fix auth bug — users staying logged in after token expires\"\n\n  7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI   feat/cache\n  \"Add Redis caching for session store\"\n```\n\n### `entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>`\n\n**Usage:**\n```\nentire prompts show a3b2c4d5e6f7      # Show full prompt for checkpoint\nentire prompts show abc123             # Short prefix accepted\n```\n\n**Output format:**\n```\nCheckpoint: a3b2c4d5e6f7\nSession: 2026-03-15-uuid\nAgent: Claude Code (claude-sonnet-4-20250514)\nBranch: main\nCreated: 2026-03-15 10:30:00\n\nPrompt:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nWhy did we choose Redis over Memcached for the caching layer?\nWe need low-latency reads for user sessions, and Memcached doesn't\nsupport clustering. Redis with Redis Cluster gives us sharding and\nautomatic failover.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nFiles touched:\n  cache/redis.go\n  cache/redis_test.go\n  config/session.yaml\n\nRun: entire checkpoint explain a3b2c4d5e6f7\nRun: entire checkpoint rewind --to a3b2c4d5e6f7\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Component Design\n\n### Package Structure\n\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n├── prompts.go       # Main command group + subcommands\n├── search.go        # Search command implementation\n├── list.go          # List command implementation\n├── show.go          # Show command implementation\n├── index.go         # Index build/update logic\n├── store.go         # Index file I/O (read/write .entire/prompts/)\n├── rank.go          # Ranking algorithm\n├── test/\n│   ├── prompts_test.go\n│   ├── search_test.go\n│   └── rank_test.go\n```\n\n### Index Store (`store.go`)\n\n**Location:** `.entire/prompts/index.json.gz`\n- Gitignored (contains local session data)\n- Compressed with gzip to reduce disk usage\n- Atomic writes (write to temp file, rename)\n\n**Operations:**\n- `LoadIndex(path string) (*PromptIndex, error)` — read index\n- `SaveIndex(path string, idx *PromptIndex) error` — write index\n- `IndexPath(repoRoot string) string` — get `.entire/prompts/index.json.gz`\n\n### Ranker (`rank.go`)\n\n**Operations:**\n- `ScoreEntry(entry PromptEntry, query string) float64` — score single entry\n- `TokenizeQuery(query string) []string` — tokenize search query\n- `TokenizePrompt(prompt string) []string` — tokenize prompt for matching\n- `Search(index *PromptIndex, query string, limit int) []SearchResult` — find matching entries\n\n### Hook Integration\n\nThe index is updated at condensation time (PostCommit hook in `manual_commit_hooks.go`).\nNew code in `prompts/index.go`:\n```go\nfunc (idx *PromptIndex) AddCheckpoint(cpID string, session SessionData) error\n```\n\nCalled from the PostCommit hook handler after `writeCommitted` succeeds.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Benchmarking\n\n### Target Performance\n\n| Operation | Target | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Index load (100 checkpoints) | < 50ms | Compressed JSON, ~50KB |\n| Index load (1000 checkpoints) | < 200ms | Compressed JSON, ~500KB |\n| Index load (10000 checkpoints) | < 1s | Compressed JSON, ~5MB |\n| Search query (100 checkpoints) | < 10ms | In-memory, no I/O |\n| Search query (1000 checkpoints) | < 50ms | In-memory, no I/O |\n| Search query (10000 checkpoints) | < 200ms | In-memory, no I/O |\n| Index build (new checkpoint) | < 100ms | Append to existing index |\n\n### Index Size Estimates\n\n| Checkpoints | Avg prompt length | Index size (compressed) |\n|-------------|-------------------|-------------------------|\n| 100 | 200 chars | ~50KB |\n| 1,000 | 200 chars | ~500KB |\n| 10,000 | 200 chars | ~5MB |\n| 100,000 | 200 chars | ~50MB |\n\n### Comparison: Index vs No Index\n\n| Checkpoints | On-demand scan | Indexed search |\n|-------------|----------------|----------------|\n| 100 | ~500ms | < 10ms |\n| 1,000 | ~5s | < 50ms |\n| 10,000 | ~50s | < 200ms |\n\n**On-demand scan is not acceptable at scale. Index is required.**\n\n---\n\n## 11. Edge Cases\n\n### 1. Missing index file\n- On first run, no index exists\n- Fall back to on-demand git tree scan\n- Build index in background, warn user results may be incomplete\n\n### 2. Corrupt index file\n- Detect via JSON parse error or magic bytes mismatch\n- Delete corrupt file, rebuild from git tree\n- Log warning: \"Index corrupted, rebuilding...\"\n\n### 3. Large prompts\n- Truncate prompt text to 2000 chars in index\n- Full prompt available via `entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>` (reads from git)\n\n### 4. Multi-session checkpoints\n- Index all sessions separately (0/, 1/, 2/)\n- Each session prompt gets its own entry\n- Display session index in results: \"Session 2 of 3\"\n\n### 5. Empty prompts\n- Skip checkpoints with empty or whitespace-only prompts\n- Log count of skipped (for debugging)\n\n### 6. Non-ASCII prompts\n- Full UTF-8 support required\n- Tokenization respects Unicode word boundaries\n- Stop words: English only (expandable)\n\n### 7. Checkpoint deleted from git\n- Index still contains old checkpoint IDs\n- On access, check if checkpoint exists in git\n- If not found, skip in search results (don't delete from index on every query)\n\n### 8. Branch renaming / rebasing\n- Branch name is metadata only, not used for sharding\n- Checkpoint ID is stable across branch operations\n- No invalidation needed\n\n### 9. Privacy / PII\n- Prompts stored in git are already redacted (PII redaction at condensation time)\n- Index uses same prompt content as git storage\n- No new data exposure\n\n### 10. Cross-repo search\n- Not supported in Phase 1\n- Future: sync index to checkpoint remote, search across repos\n\n---\n\n## 12. Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Core (MVP)\n\n**Week 1:**\n- Create `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/` package\n- Implement index store (`store.go`) — read/write compressed JSON\n- Implement index builder (`index.go`) — addCheckpoint from session data\n- Implement ranker (`rank.go`) — keyword matching + scoring\n- Add PostCommit hook integration to update index\n\n**Week 2:**\n- Implement `entire prompts list` command\n- Implement `entire prompts search` command\n- Implement `entire prompts show` command\n- Add basic tests\n\n**Week 3:**\n- Add `--limit`, `--agent`, `--branch`, `--after` filters\n- Add `--json` output\n- Add interactive mode (Bubble Tea TUI)\n- Performance testing and optimization\n\n### Phase 2: Enhanced (Future)\n\n- Add TF-IDF ranking for better relevance\n- Add file context in results (show which files prompt touched)\n- Add session threading (show multi-turn conversations)\n- Performance optimization (lazy loading, pagination)\n\n### Phase 3: Semantic (Future)\n\n- Add embedding generation (local or API)\n- Implement hybrid search (BM25 + dense retrieval)\n- Add privacy controls (exclude sensitive repos)\n\n---\n\n## 13. Open Questions\n\n1. **Index rebuild on migration?** — If user migrates from v1 to v2 checkpoints, should we rebuild index?\n2. **Prompt truncation length?** — 2000 chars is an estimate. What's the real distribution?\n3. **Stop word list?** — English stop words only for now. Add more languages later?\n4. **Interactive mode?** — Bubble Tea TUI for search with pager, or stick to CLI output?\n5. **Integration with `entire search`?** — Should `entire search --prompts` delegate to this?\n\n---\n\n## 14. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `entire prompts search <query>` returns relevant prompts in < 200ms for 10K checkpoints\n- [ ] `entire prompts list` shows recent prompts with checkpoint IDs\n- [ ] `entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>` shows full prompt text\n- [ ] Index is updated automatically on every commit\n- [ ] Works offline without internet\n- [ ] No new external dependencies (no CGO, no SQLite)\n- [ ] Tests cover ranking algorithm and edge cases\n- [ ] Performance: index load < 1s for 10K checkpoints\n\n---\n\n## 15. References\n\n1. [Entire Roadmap Blog](https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed)\n2. `checkpoint/checkpoint.go` — Checkpoint types\n3. `checkpoint/committed.go` — Committed checkpoint I/O\n4. `strategy/common.go` — ReadSessionPromptFromTree, ExtractFirstPrompt\n5. `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go` — PostCommit hook (where to integrate index update)\n6. `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/` — New package (to be created)",
