              "command": "gh issue edit 1187 --body '## Problem\n\nDevelopers can search **what changed** (`git blame`, `grep`) but cannot search **why it changed** — the prompts and reasoning behind decisions. Today that context lives in closed terminal sessions and disappears on close.\n\n> \"We're making that answer searchable. Users will be able to surface the prompt that introduced a workaround or revisit the reasoning behind a library choice months later. The 'why' will be part of your history.\" — [Entire Roadmap](https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed)\n\n**Example:** \"Why did we pick Redis over Memcached?\"\n- `grep redis` → finds usage, not decision\n- `git blame` → shows who changed it, not why\n- Slack / Notion → fragmented, not tied to commits\n\n**With searchable prompts:**\n```\n$ entire prompts search \"cache decision\"\n→ \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached?\"   a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code\n→ \"Add Redis caching for session store\"        7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI\n```\n\n## Roadmap Alignment\n\n| Feature | Status | Roadmap Section |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Searchable Prompts** | NOT SHIPPED | \"Search\" — surfacing the prompt that introduced a workaround |\n| Intent Review | NOT SHIPPED | \"Rethinking Code Review to Intent Review\" |\n| Team Visibility | NOT SHIPPED | \"Team Visibility\" |\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\n**New command family:**\n```\nentire prompts search <query>   # Search prompts by keywords\nentire prompts list            # List recent prompts\nentire prompts show <id>       # Show full prompt for a checkpoint\nentire prompts index --rebuild # Rebuild index from git\n```\n\n**Implementation approach:** Persistent local index (`.ndjson` in `.entire/prompts/`) — offline-first, no new external deps, no CGO.\n\n### Key design decisions:\n\n- **Storage:** `.ndjson` (newline-delimited JSON) — appendable, no compression overhead, ~650KB for 1K checkpoints\n- **Algorithm:** Porter stemmer (pure Go, `github.com/kljensen/snowball`) + weighted keyword scoring. Not BM25 (requires IDF across corpus; overkill for local index)\n- **Index update:** At PostCommit hook (condensation time) — incrementally updated, never requires a full rebuild in steady state\n- **Cold start:** `entire prompts index --rebuild` walks `entire/checkpoints/v1` git tree with a progress bar. Auto-triggers on first search if index is missing.\n- **Multi-turn:** `prompt.txt` stores multi-turn conversations split by `\"---\\n\\n\"`. Each turn is indexed as a separate entry with `TurnIndex`\n- **Agent review prompts:** `CommittedMetadata.ReviewPrompt` is also indexed with `Kind: \"agent_review\"`\n- **Concurrency:** File lock with retry backoff for concurrent writes. NFS fallback to PID-lock file.\n- **Benchmarks:** Search < 20ms for 1K, < 100ms for 10K. Index load < 100ms for 1K.\n\n### Performance comparison:\n\n| Checkpoints | On-demand scan | Indexed search |\n|---|---|---|\n| 100 | ~500ms | < 10ms |\n| 1,000 | ~5s | < 20ms |\n| 10,000 | ~50s | < 100ms |\n\n## What This Does NOT Cover\n\n- Cross-repo search (Phase 3+)\n- Semantic/embedding search (Phase 3+)\n- Integration with web platform\n- Non-English stop words\n\n## Commands\n\n### `entire prompts search`\n```\nentire prompts search \"redis cache\"\nentire prompts search --limit 50\nentire prompts search --json\nentire prompts search --agent claude\nentire prompts search --branch feat/auth\nentire prompts search --after 2026-03-01\nentire prompts search --kind agent_review\n```\n\n### `entire prompts index`\n```\nentire prompts index --rebuild   # full rebuild with progress bar\nentire prompts index --status   # checkpoint count, prompt count, orphan count\nentire prompts index --verify    # check for orphaned entries\n```\n\n## Package Structure\n\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n├── prompts.go        # Command group\n├── search.go         # entire prompts search\n├── list.go           # entire prompts list\n├── show.go           # entire prompts show\n├── index_cmd.go      # entire prompts index\n└── index/\n    ├── schema.go     # IndexHeader, PromptEntry types\n    ├── store.go      # read/append/rebuild, file locking\n    ├── builder.go    # walk checkpoint tree, multi-turn parsing\n    └── rank.go       # tokenizer, stemmer, scorer\n```\n\n## Open Questions\n\n1. Should `entire search` (code, external API) and `entire prompts search` eventually be unified into one umbrella command?\n2. Progress bar pattern — use existing Bubble Tea components or simple `fmt.Printf`?\n3. Prompt truncation at 2000 chars — what's the real p95 in existing checkpoint data?\n4. Which agents run PII redaction at condensation time? Need to verify before shipping.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `entire prompts search` < 100ms for 1K checkpoints, < 500ms for 10K\n- [ ] Stemming active — \"caching\" matches \"cache\"\n- [ ] Multi-turn conversations indexed per-turn\n- [ ] `--json` in non-TTY emits PII warning to stderr\n- [ ] Concurrent writes do not corrupt index\n- [ ] Cold start auto-rebuild works with progress bar\n- [ ] No new CGO dependencies\n- [ ] All benchmark targets met\n\n## References\n\n- [Roadmap Blog](https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed)\n- Feature proposal: [docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md](docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md)\n- Key existing code: `checkpoint/committed.go`, `strategy/common.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`'",
