              "file": "docs/FEATURE_prompts_search.md",
              "patch": "Index: docs/FEATURE_prompts_search.md\n===================================================================\n--- docs/FEATURE_prompts_search.md\t\n+++ docs/FEATURE_prompts_search.md\t\n@@ -0,0 +1,363 @@\n+# Feature: Searchable Prompts CLI (`entire prompts`)\n+\n+**Source of truth for implementation.** All decisions, design choices, and acceptance criteria are documented here. Update this doc when decisions change.\n+\n+- **GitHub Issue:** #1187\n+- **Roadmap:** https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed\n+- **Feature Proposal:** `docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 1. Problem\n+\n+Developers can search **what changed** but cannot search **why it changed** — the prompts and reasoning behind decisions.\n+\n+> \"We're making that answer searchable. Users will be able to surface the prompt that introduced a workaround or revisit the reasoning behind a library choice months later. The 'why' will be part of your history.\" — Entire Roadmap\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Scope\n+\n+### In Scope (Phase 1)\n+- `entire prompts search <query>` — keyword search over prompt history\n+- `entire prompts list` — list recent prompts\n+- `entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>` — show full prompt from git\n+- `entire prompts index` — rebuild / status / verify\n+\n+### Out of Scope\n+- Cross-repo search\n+- Semantic/embedding search\n+- Web platform integration\n+- Non-English stop words\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Architecture\n+\n+### Index Design\n+\n+**File:** `.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` (gitignored, local to this checkout)\n+\n+**Why `.ndjson` over JSON:**\n+- gzip is a stream format — cannot append to it. Every update would require full read → decompress → modify → compress → rewrite.\n+- `.ndjson` is appendable — new entries are single-line appends, no full rewrites.\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```go\n+// Header — first line of the file\n+type IndexHeader struct {\n+    Version   int       `json:\"version\"`    // format version (1)\n+    CreatedAt time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n+    RepoRoot  string    `json:\"repo_root\"`  // sanity check\n+}\n+\n+// Each subsequent line is one entry\n+type PromptEntry struct {\n+    CheckpointID      string    `json:\"checkpoint_id\"`    // \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\"\n+    SessionIndex      int       `json:\"session_index\"`    // 0, 1, 2 (multi-session)\n+    TurnIndex         int       `json:\"turn_index\"`       // 0, 1, 2 (multi-turn)\n+    Kind              string    `json:\"kind\"`             // \"session\" | \"agent_review\"\n+    PromptText        string    `json:\"prompt_text\"`      // truncated to 2000 chars\n+    PromptTruncated   bool      `json:\"prompt_truncated\"`\n+    CommitHash        string    `json:\"commit_hash\"`\n+    CommitMessage     string    `json:\"commit_message\"`   // first line only\n+    Branch            string    `json:\"branch\"`\n+    Agent             string    `json:\"agent\"`            // \"Claude Code\"\n+    Model             string    `json:\"model\"`\n+    TokenCount        int       `json:\"token_count\"`\n+    ParentCheckpointID string  `json:\"parent_checkpoint_id,omitempty\"`\n+    SubagentDepth     int       `json:\"subagent_depth\"`\n+    FilesTouched      []string  `json:\"files_touched\"`\n+    CreatedAt         time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Index version constant:**\n+```go\n+const CurrentIndexVersion = 1\n+```\n+\n+**Version migration:** On `version < CurrentIndexVersion` or parse error, delete index and rebuild.\n+\n+### Package Structure\n+\n+```\n+cmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n+├── prompts.go        # Command group registration\n+├── search.go         # entire prompts search\n+├── list.go           # entire prompts list\n+├── show.go           # entire prompts show\n+├── index_cmd.go      # entire prompts index\n+└── index/\n+    ├── schema.go     # IndexHeader, PromptEntry types\n+    ├── store.go      # read/append/rebuild, file locking\n+    ├── builder.go    # walk checkpoint tree, multi-turn parsing\n+    └── rank.go       # tokenizer, stemmer, scorer\n+```\n+\n+### Multi-Worktree Support\n+\n+Index lives at `<worktree-git-dir>/../.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` so concurrent worktrees have independent indexes.\n+\n+### Decoupled Checkpoint Repo\n+\n+When `checkpoint.remote` is configured, `IndexPath()` reads that config to resolve the checkpoint repo location.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 4. Search Algorithm\n+\n+### Tokenizer\n+\n+```go\n+func Tokenize(text string) []string {\n+    // 1. Unicode normalization (NFC)\n+    normalized := norm.NFC.String(strings.ToLower(text))\n+    // 2. Split on non-word characters (regex)\n+    tokens := wordBoundary.Split(normalized, -1)\n+    // 3. Stem each token (Porter stemmer)\n+    stemmed := make([]string, 0, len(tokens))\n+    for _, t := range tokens {\n+        if len(t) < 2 { continue }       // skip single chars\n+        if stopWords[t] { continue }       // skip stop words\n+        stemmed = append(stemmed, stem.Stem(t))\n+    }\n+    return stemmed\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Stemmer:** `github.com/kljensen/snowball` — pure Go, zero CGO, MIT license.\n+\n+**Why stemming matters:**\n+- `\"caching\"` → stems to `\"cach\"` → matches `\"cache\"`, `\"cached\"`, `\"caches\"`\n+- `\"authenticated\"` → stems to `\"authent\"` → matches `\"auth\"`, `\"authentication\"`\n+- Without stemming, ~30–40% of valid matches return zero results\n+\n+### Scorer\n+\n+Weighted keyword scoring with term-density normalization:\n+\n+```\n+TermDensity = matched_token_count / total_prompt_token_count\n+\n+Score = (exact_phrase_match * 10)\n+      + (all_query_tokens_found * 5)\n+      + (any_query_token_found * 1)\n+      + (TermDensity * 2)\n+```\n+\n+**Within same score tier:** newer `CreatedAt` first.\n+\n+**Minimum query length:** 2 characters after tokenization. Early return with error: `\"query too short — enter at least one word\"`.\n+\n+**Special character handling:** Strip regex metacharacters before tokenization. Not interpreted as patterns.\n+\n+**Quoted phrase handling:** `\"redis cache\"` parsed as phrase, matched as adjacent sequence in stemmed token stream.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Commands\n+\n+### `entire prompts search`\n+\n+```\n+entire prompts search <query>\n+entire prompts search \"redis cache\"\n+entire prompts search --limit 50\n+entire prompts search --json\n+entire prompts search --agent claude\n+entire prompts search --branch feat/auth\n+entire prompts search --after 2026-03-01\n+entire prompts search --files cache/redis.go\n+entire prompts search --kind agent_review\n+```\n+\n+**Output:**\n+```\n+Search results for \"redis cache\"  (23 found, showing 20)\n+\n+  a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code  main\n+  \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached for the caching layer?\"\n+\n+  7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI   feat/cache\n+  \"Add Redis caching for session store to improve latency\"\n+```\n+\n+### `entire prompts list`\n+\n+```\n+entire prompts list               # last 20, newest first\n+entire prompts list --limit 50\n+entire prompts list --checkpoint abc123\n+entire prompts list --cursor <token>   # cursor-based pagination\n+```\n+\n+### `entire prompts show`\n+\n+```\n+entire prompts show a3b2c4d5e6f7\n+entire prompts show abc123              # prefix accepted\n+```\n+\n+**Ambiguous prefix:** If short prefix matches multiple, list matches and ask to disambiguate.\n+\n+### `entire prompts index`\n+\n+```\n+entire prompts index --rebuild   # full rebuild with progress bar\n+entire prompts index --status    # checkpoint count, prompt count, orphans\n+entire prompts index --verify    # check for orphaned entries\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. Data Flow\n+\n+### Index Update (at PostCommit hook)\n+\n+```\n+User commits → PostCommit hook fires\n+      ↓\n+strategy.Condense() → WriteCommitted() writes checkpoint to git\n+      ↓\n+prompts.IndexBuilder.AppendFromCheckpoint(cpID, sessionIndex, sessionData)\n+      ↓\n+Acquire file lock (.entire/prompts/index.lock)\n+Append PromptEntry line to index.ndjson\n+Release lock\n+```\n+\n+### Query (at search command)\n+\n+```\n+entire prompts search \"redis cache\"\n+      ↓\n+LoadIndex() — read index.ndjson line by line\n+  If missing → rebuild → reload\n+  If version mismatch or parse error → rebuild → reload\n+      ↓\n+ParseQuery() → handle quotes, strip special chars\n+TokenizeQuery() → stem, remove stop words\n+      ↓\n+Score each PromptEntry (in-memory, no I/O after load)\n+Apply filters (--agent, --branch, --after, --files, --kind)\n+Sort by score desc, then CreatedAt desc\n+Slice to --limit\n+      ↓\n+FormatResults() → TTY or JSON\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. Edge Cases\n+\n+| # | Case | Handling |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| 1 | Missing index | Auto-rebuild with progress bar, warn results may lag |\n+| 2 | Corrupt index (parse error) | Delete, rebuild, log notice |\n+| 3 | Index version mismatch | Delete, rebuild automatically |\n+| 4 | Large prompts (>2000 chars) | Truncate in index, set `PromptTruncated=true` |\n+| 5 | Match past truncation point | Result shown with note |\n+| 6 | Multi-turn conversations | Each turn indexed separately with `TurnIndex` |\n+| 7 | Agent review prompts | Indexed with `Kind=\"agent_review\"`, filterable with `--kind` |\n+| 8 | Subagent checkpoints | `ParentCheckpointID` and `SubagentDepth` set |\n+| 9 | Empty prompts | Skipped, count logged in `--status` |\n+| 10 | Non-ASCII / Unicode | NFC normalization, `\"café\"` matches `\"cafe\"` |\n+| 11 | Special chars in query | Stripped, not interpreted as regex |\n+| 12 | Query too short | Early return with error |\n+| 13 | Checkpoint deleted from git | `--verify` detects orphans, search skips silently |\n+| 14 | Concurrent writes | File lock with retry backoff; NFS fallback to PID-lock |\n+| 15 | Prefix ambiguity | List matches, prompt disambiguation |\n+| 16 | `--json` in non-TTY | PII warning to stderr |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 8. Concurrency\n+\n+### File Lock Pattern\n+\n+```go\n+func (s *IndexStore) AppendEntry(entry PromptEntry